{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEach sidecar payload is keyed by `(change_id, revision)`\n(`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py:99-101`) and Gerrit emits one `code_review` artifact ticket\nper revision (`src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py:84`). A finding raised on one\npatchset and not re-emitted on the next reaches no consumer — the change merges on the reviewer's\nsilence. On change 1867 the `assert elapsed < 10` wall-clock advisory ran on PS1-PS2, vanished on\nPS3-PS4, which merged `LLM-Review+1` with zero findings; the defect then broke macOS CI on 1869\n(re-found as bug `9bb7-4430-1202-4d93`). Reviewer recall is non-deterministic per run. Approved\n2026-08-21.\n\nMemory exists but is narrow: `latest_code_review_result(\"change:<id>\")` (`sidecar.py:332`) spans\nrevisions and `apply_region_gated_floor` (`workflow_ops.py:634`) consumes it only to **narrow** the\nverdict, stamping `carried_from` on a finding the fresh run re-emitted (`:682-686`). Nothing\nre-raises one the fresh run dropped.\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror plan-review's recall backstop (`llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:355-495`) — no second mechanism.\nPaths omit `src/rebar/`.\n\n- **Reader.** `sidecar.standing_items(key, *, repo_root)` reads the prior payload via\n  `latest_code_review_result`, extended to also return `revision` (today\n  `{findings, deps, session_id, change_id}`, `:388-393`) so each item knows its origin patchset.\n  Capped by `STANDING_CAP`.\n- **Surfaced-only.** `build_payload` persists `dropped`/`indeterminate` beside `blocking`/`advisory`\n  (`sidecar.py:108-111`); `latest_code_review_result` unions only `blocking` + `advisory` and\n  `standing_items` must NOT widen it: that resurrects findings the region-gated floor permanently\n  dropped (bug `old-frilly-plankton`).\n- **Grounded-only.** An evidence-less item gives the verifier nothing to re-ground, so re-grounding\n  becomes confirming a bare assertion and its residue seeds replays forever (bug\n  `deceitful-flannel-jerboa`); carried evidence terminates the chain.\n- **Injection point.** At Pass-1 assembly, NOT `finalize.py` (docstring `:1-9`: it runs only after a\n  terminal verdict). Items whose `norm_id` fresh Pass-1 did not produce are\n  appended by `merge_findings` (`workflow_ops.py:226`), flowing into `code_review_verify_inputs`\n  (`:262`) — plan-review's seam (`pass1.py:373-374`); finders never see them.\n- **Shared kernel: no behaviour change.** The verifier's listing comes from\n  `review_kernel.verify_instructions` (`review_kernel/verify.py:114`), which **plan-review also\n  calls** (`plan_review/passes.py:66`) — so standing-item wording goes in a code-review-local wrapper\n  inside `code_review_verify_inputs` and in the Pass-2 prompt `llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md`,\n  and `verify.py` changes only `prior_findings_block`'s now-wrong docstring claim that the novelty\n  sub-call is \"the ONLY place the prior findings appear\" (`:435`).\n- **State.** Each item is recorded `still-present`, `addressed`, or `withdrawn` on a new `standing`\n  sub-object (`{origin_revision, state}`) — an additive key on the finding and the buckets that\n  persist it; no `disposition` field exists today.\n- **Posture clamp (pinned, not assumed).** `pass3_decide` RECOMPUTES `decision` every run as \"BLOCK\n  iff blocking_enabled AND priority >= block_threshold\" (`review_kernel/decide.py:653, :730`), the\n  threshold resolved per criterion from `criteria_routing.json` (`workflow_ops.py:423`) where eight\n  criteria are `blocking_enabled: true`; and on 1867 the defect changed criterion between patch sets.\n  So `code_review_decide` clamps a finding carrying `standing` to at most its origin decision. The\n  region-gated floor is unaffected: a standing item scores near-zero novelty, so\n  `rising_floor_drop` (`decide.py:105`) cannot drop it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `llm/code_review/sidecar.py` — `standing_items()`, `STANDING_CAP`; `latest_code_review_result` also\n  returns `revision`.\n- `llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py` — inject in `merge_findings` (`:226`); listing in\n  `code_review_verify_inputs` (`:262`); clamp in `code_review_decide` (`:386`). **712 LOC vs the 800\n  cap** (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`); if it crosses, split the carry-forward cluster to\n  `llm/code_review/carry_forward.py` along the existing merge/verify seam.\n- `llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md` — standing-item rubric (the Pass-2 prompt; no\n  `code-review-verifier.md` exists).\n- `llm/review_kernel/verify.py` — docstring only.\n- `review_bot/artifact_emit.py` — Gerrit-path `sidecar.emit` (`:114`); output unchanged, but the\n  standing chain is auditable only here.\n- `review_bot/adapter.py` — `_translate_findings` (`:122`) drops keys outside\n  `{severity, dimension, detail, location}`; carry `standing` through it.\n- `review_bot/finding_publish.py` — `render_findings_block` (`:126`), `build_inline_comments`\n  (`:147`) render \"since patchset k\"; Gerrit text is composed here, not `adapter.py`.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py` (new) — flat layout; no `tests/unit/llm/`.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_region_gate.py` — stubs monkeypatch\n  `\"rebar.llm.code_review.sidecar.latest_code_review_result\"` **by string** at `:85`, `:183`, `:201`\n  (and `test_code_review_gate_session.py:484`); add `revision` there or the floor reads a stale\n  shape.\n\n## Testing\n\nCases: cited lines deleted -> `addressed`; first review -> none; empty `evidence` -> ineligible (a\nreplay cannot seed another); `dropped` bucket -> never carried; rebase-only -> all kept; a\n`blocking_enabled` criterion above its `block_threshold` -> still advisory.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Reader exists, surfaced-only + grounded-only: `python -c \"from rebar.llm.code_review.sidecar import standing_items, STANDING_CAP\"` exits 0, and `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -q` passes — incl. the `dropped`-bucket and evidence-less cases yielding zero items.\n- [ ] A finding on revision N-1 absent from fresh Pass-1 on N appears in N's sidecar with `standing.state` and `standing.origin_revision`: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -k sidecar_records_standing_state -q`.\n- [ ] Prior-payload reader exposes `revision`: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py -k latest_code_review_result -q` passes with an added assertion for `revision`.\n- [ ] Carry-forward never raises a posture, incl. a `blocking_enabled` criterion: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -k posture_clamp -q` passes.\n- [ ] The Pass-2 prompt in Scope exists: `test -f src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md && grep -c \"standing\" src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md` returns a count ≥ 1.\n- [ ] The shared kernel listing builder is unchanged (plan-review's verifier untouched): `git diff --stat origin/main -- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py` shows docstring-only lines, and `pytest tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py tests/unit/test_review_kernel_rules.py tests/unit/test_verify_empty_batch_contract.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_novelty.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] Gerrit messages show carried findings \"since patchset k\": `grep -n \"since patchset\" src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py` returns at least one line, and `pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] The convergence path is not regressed and its stubs are updated: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_region_gate.py tests/unit/test_code_review_gate_session.py tests/unit/test_code_review_finalize.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] Repo gates hold: every touched `src/rebar` file is at or under `.github/module-size-limit.txt` (`for f in $(git diff --name-only origin/main -- 'src/rebar/**/*.py'); do test \"$(wc -l < $f)\" -le \"$(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt)\" || exit 1; done` exits 0), and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports no `new` or `increased` entries."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787371667594194001,"uuid":"00b2a314-8cde-4912-935f-6c0ee5d2a77c"}